            "level": {
              "value": 1
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "When you trick a foe, instead of catching them off guard, you goad them into overextending their next attack. On a successful Feint, you can use the following success and critical success effects instead of any other effects that would occur when you Feint. You can choose a different effect each time you Feint against a given foe.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to all attack rolls against you before the end of its next turn.\n- **Success:** The target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its next attack roll against you before the end of its next turn."
            }
          }
        }
